Q: How to create an empty array of a given size? A: <p>I'm not sure what was the underlying purpose of the initial question, but I needed something like this to have an array as an &quot;expression&quot; to &quot;map&quot; it inside a React component to achieve something like &quot;for&quot; which we can't use in a JSX markup.</p>
<p>Josh W. Comeau recommends using a &quot;range&quot; utility function for this purpose:</p>
<p><a href="https://www.joshwcomeau.com/snippets/javascript/range/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Generate a &quot;range&quot; array in JavaScript</a></p>
<p>That would be great if this was a built-in JS function.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const range = (start, end, step = 1) =&gt; {
  let output = [];

  if (typeof end === 'undefined') {
    end = start;
    start = 0;
  }

  for (let i = start; i &lt; end; i += step) {
    output.push(i);
  }

  return output;
};

//Sample usage:
range(10).map((num) =&gt; console.log(num));</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Query Nested Array in Cosmos DB A: <p>Here is the sample query</p>
<pre><code>SELECT c.id, c.PartitionKey
FROM c
JOIN t IN c.Fees
where array_contains(t.Tags,&quot;test-1&quot;)
</code></pre>
